// Typecheck the tests.
//
// `tsconfig.json` excludes `src/**/tests/**` because tests must not reach the
// published `dist/`. That exclusion also meant the tests were never typechecked
// at all, and a test that does not typecheck is a test that can assert against
// an interface the module no longer has. It hid a real one for a release: when
// `TraceStore.append` started returning `AppendAck`, a decorator in
// `guardrails/tests/production.test.ts` still declared `Promise<RecordedNode>`,
// and `npm run check` was green.
//
// So the tests get their own pass: same strictness, no emit, no `composite`,
// nothing written to disk. It is wired into `npm run check` as
// `typecheck:tests`, after the build and before the tests themselves run —
// a type error here fails the gate rather than waiting for someone to notice.
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "sourceMap": false
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"]
}
